    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You need to check your passports carefully, but remember that even a single misplaced stamp can cause a whole group of engineers to get stuck in a transit zone like a confused flock of goblins trying to find the exit. For Vietnam and Thailand, the rules are strict, so you must verify if your 6 engineers qualify for visa-free transit or if they need an actual entry visa before they even board the plane. Singapore and Malaysia are generally friendlier, but a quick check at the airport information desk is essential because a goblin might be hiding in the corner of the terminal waiting to cause a scene if you don't have the right paperwork. Make sure everyone has their e-visa or visa on arrival approval printed out, because a goblin without a ticket will just stand there and stare at you until you give them the correct documents. Finally, double-check the layover times, as a goblin might try to sneak out of the airport during a short stopover, so ensure your transit windows are long enough to avoid any last-minute panic.",
